(- Cement content shall not be less than 320 kg/m³ of concrete.) Tj T*
(- OPC 43 grade cement as per IS 269:2015 shall be used.) Tj T*
(- Aggregates shall comply with the requirements of IS 383:2016.) Tj T*
(- High strength deformed bars of grade Fe 500D as per IS 1786:2008 shall be used.) Tj T*
(- Mix design shall be carried out in accordance with IS 10262:2019.) Tj T*
(- Concrete shall be kept continuously moist for at least 10 days.) Tj T*
(- Compaction shall be done by immersion vibrators.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(5 TESTS AND INSPECTION) Tj T*
(- Cube tests for compressive strength shall be done in accordance with IS 516 \(Part) Tj T*
(1/Sec 1\):2021.) Tj T*
(- Mill test certificates for steel and test certificates for cement shall be submitted) Tj T*
(for every consignment.) Tj T*
(- Pre-dispatch inspection shall be offered to the Department's authorised representative) Tj T*
(with 15 days notice.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(6 DOCUMENTATION, WARRANTY AND TRAINING) Tj T*
(- Shop drawings and schematic diagrams shall be got approved from the Engineer-in-charge) Tj T*
(before manufacture.) Tj T*
(- O&M manuals, as-built drawings and catalogues shall be furnished in triplicate at the) Tj T*
(time of handing over.) Tj T*
(- The supplier shall replace free of cost any part found defective within the defect) Tj T*
(liability period of 24 months.) Tj T*
